Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-28-2000||05:39 PM||||Please forgive my ignorance, but what are the numbers/letters on your windows??  And why would you let someone do that? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||06-28-2000||09:32 PM||||Monkeyman,<BR>  They always do that at the race track.  It identifies your car to the tower operator and it also shows what class you are in.  The 209 and 212 are probably the car number and the X and T/T identify the class the car is in.<P>   The marker they use is harmless.  Is washes off easily.  I think this method of marking the cars is more acceptable than a plywood sign attached with screws or pop rivets.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||06-29-2000||12:36 PM||||1FST, we're sitting at 1441ft here in Sioux Falls.  The track here is almost almost cool w/dense air because we're just east of the Missouri River.  The 3.1 you see in the pics is a really quick car.  The real kicker is, that engine came out of a minivan with 270,000 miles on it!!!  All the did was freshen up the bearings.  He's got a few performance goodies but nothing major.  It sounds like the car wouldn't be fast at all, but it hauls ass.  You can meet the guy when you come up.  He just registered on the forum as FIEROGOD(as a joke of course), but I haven't seen him post yet.  We've never raced from a dead stop, but we goofed around once on our way to the track.  We hit it from about 60-90 and I could barely pull away.  From a dead stop he'd have me though, because I've seen his car accelerate.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||06-29-2000||12:56 PM||||SWEET! the dyno is at like 1108ft.. so my numbers will be close to what you've been driving at... You'll be able to take him in the SE... just as long as theres a gas station on the way and your not racing to 150... with the new tranny its quicker to 60 but falls on it's face above 110... and the damn head light doors still fly up! See ya saturday morning... ||||reg||1
